        <title type="html"><![CDATA[fix(update-browser-releases): link Chrome 155+ release notes to Chrome Status]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30881</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30881"/>
        <updated>2026-10-15T15:29:54.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=9d0bf7e5c07194485c7f81827005599ecced9712&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">Makes the Chrome release updater link Chrome Status release notes for Chrome 155 and later, and adds the missing Chrome Status links for Chrome 155 to 158 in <code class="notranslate">chrome.json</code> and <code class="notranslate">chrome_android.json</code>.</p>
<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Selects the release-notes source by version: Chrome Status from 155, developer.chrome.com release notes for 124 to 154, and new-in-chrome posts for 54 to 123.</li>
<li>Chrome 155's developer.chrome.com page returns 404, so the previous lookup recorded no link. <code class="notranslate">chromestatus.com/release-notes/155</code> returns 200.</li>
<li>Adds links for 156 to 158 (beta, nightly, planned). The updater only records links for stable releases, so these are hand-added, matching the existing planned Firefox entries.</li>
</ul>
<h4 dir="auto">Related issues</h4>
<p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #30877.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5865923718" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30877" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30877/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30877">#30877</a>.</p>]]></content>
