        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Add Notifications API `navigate` option]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30781</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30781"/>
        <updated>2026-10-08T11:50:42.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>
<h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">Firefox 158 adds support for <code class="notranslate">Notification.navigator</code> — the ability to specify a URL to navigate to once a notification is clicked.</p>
<p dir="auto"><a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5714299430" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30755" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30755/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30755">#30755</a> adds <code class="notranslate">api.Notification.navigate</code> (the property), but there are two more data points required:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><code class="notranslate">api.Notification.Notification.navigate</code> (the constructor option)</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">api.ServiceWorkerRegistration.showNotification.options_navigate_parameter</code> (the service worker <code class="notranslate">showNotification()</code> option)</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">This PR adds both.</p>

